Two concrete risk areas are emerging: the merge path holds the entire records system’s write lock while the source-control operation runs, and its “all-or-nothing” claim cannot survive a database commit failure after the merge has already succeeded. I’m now checking the panel’s late-answer reconciliation and the exact review-floor arithmetic before deciding severity.
